    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0450" n="446" xml:id="pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/1498: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-22T18:00:00+09:00">February 22, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 22—7:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. The German Chargé told me that he called this morning on the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs<anchor n="89" xml:id="d427-f1"/> and stated, under instructions
                    from his Government, that Germany will recognize Manchukuo.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for Hankow and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d427-f1" n="89" xml:id="d427-f1-content">
                <p>Koki Hirota.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
